  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 306 PM EDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nSunday - Monday...\n\nThe upper ridge breaks down a bit across the southern CONUS to end \nthe weekend. As a result, a belt of slightly stronger westerlies \nsinks a bit southward from the Corn Belt through the mid Atlantic. A \nsurface front will also accompany this southward shift as it settles \ninto the Ohio River Valley region by Monday morning. \n\nWe'll still be hot and muggy on Sunday ahead of the boundary as it \napproaches, however it looks like it will be displaced to the north \nenough to not be a factor on Sunday. In addition, we'll likely still \nhave enough influence from the weakening upper ridge to keep the \narea dry. Given Max Ts and the low and mid 90s and dew points in the \n65 to 70 degree range, we'll still see max heat indices in the 95 to \n100 F range on Sunday.\n\nBy Monday, the front does sink into the area with cooler \ntemperatures in the low and mid 80s across our northern CWA, but \nstill in the upper 80s and low 90s across southern KY. We'll also \nhave scattered afternoon and evening showers and storms triggered by \nboth the frontal boundary and perhaps some subtle embedded shortwave \nactivity passing through the flow. \n\nTuesday - Wednesday...\n\nThe real cool down sets in through mid week as a notable shortwave \nrotates through the lower Great Lakes and Ohio River Valley region. \nThe aforementioned surface front will push south of the area with \nmuch cooler temperatures in the 75-80 degree range across southern \nIN and northern KY, and in the 80-85 degree range across southern \nKY. We'll also have pretty good coverage of showers and storms (up \nto 70% east of I-65) on Tuesday ahead of the shortwave trough axis. \nBy Wednesday, the shortwave trough axis will be slowly pushing east \nof the area, but will likely be still carrying pops across our \neastern CWA, with better chances for drier weather across the \nwestern CWA. Temps will even be cooler by Wednesday with low and mid \n70s north, and highs near 80 across southern KY.\n\nThursday - Friday...\n\nGood chance that we get back into dry NW flow aloft for late week. \nThis should be a drier pattern, with temperatures mostly in the mid \nand upper 70s. It should be noted that the mid to late week \"cool \ndown\" really just ends up being temperatures back close to normal \nfor this time of year, maybe slightly below on a couple of the days.",
